{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay","id":1547463,"title":"How do you see dominated characters roleplay?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-02T12:56:20-08:00","id":1547463,"title":"How do you see dominated characters roleplay?","content":"So, I'm here again wanting to know other's ST opinion. How do you roleplay (or tell the players to roleplay) when the PCs are dominated by another cainite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T21:24:21-08:00","id":1547473,"title":"","content":"We personally see dominated characters acting normal until a key word or person shows up and it comes into play and they feel compelled to act a certain way. With me I would use the Dominate Discipline to condition the subject to report what they saw and heard and give me regular updates and if I wanted to cover my tracks more. Maybe I would pose as another Kindred and they take the blame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T21:38:26-08:00","id":1547475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay?p=1547473#post1547473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We personally see dominated characters acting normal until a key word or person shows up and it comes into play and they feel compelled to act a certain way. With me I would use the Dominate Discipline to condition the subject to report what they saw and heard and give me regular updates and if I wanted to cover my tracks more. Maybe I would pose as another Kindred and they take the blame.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, from the outside I understand what you mean. I think perhaps I haven't explained well what I meant. The question is more related to <i>how</i> you as a ST normally make they act. For instance, I often describe the scene when it happens, like, for instance: &quot; You've heard Herr Brandt saying 'kneel' while staring into your eyes and you're now on your knees in front of him, feeling a bit confused...&quot;, just to cite an example, while other times I've allowed the player to roleplay the action himself, I mean there are some differeces in regards to the approach. In fact nowadays I'm more convinced that with <i>Dominate</i> it's probably better to make it happen this way as it's a rather forced action, unlike, for instance, Presence, where you basically have to let the player roleplay (as long as he acts according to how the character should feel, ofc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T23:12:55-08:00","id":1547477,"title":"","content":"I would say it really depends on the level of Dominate being used.<br /> <br /> A character who has an implanted command/suggestion does not have to know that it is there, only becoming aware of it once it activates. Thus, you can have some very interesting &quot;Manchurian Candidate&quot; style shenanigans going on. You can make a whole game of the coterie trying to figure out what the trigger conditions are and based on that they then can try to guess who implanted them.<br /> <br /> Likewise, since memory manipulation is a thing, you can play it out like each PCs backstory is essentially an unreliable narrator. Though I find that on both a mechanical level and a storytelling level, it works best to change details rather than large chunks of memory. This way when they go digging through their notes, the players don't always catch the change and just go with it.<br /> <br /> As for the first power, unless it's used in an obvious fashion like forcing someone to kneel, it can be concealed inside a normal sentence with perhaps a hint of emphasis. For example, if the Dominate user is playing poker and says to one of the other players &quot;you should <b><i>Fold</i></b> this hand&quot; the target will do so but then be confused as to why they did that.<br /> <br /> If you are planning on running a dominate heavy game, it might be helpful to pull the targeted player aside ahead of time to work out what might happen. This won't always make for the best role play by that player, but it does make for much better role play for the rest of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T06:45:13-08:00","id":1547487,"title":"","content":"&quot;These are not the droids you're looking for...&quot; -style<br /> From the Dominated perspective they are most of the time not even aware they are under some &quot;spell&quot; - especially if they are young cainites and just heard rumors about the power<br /> A smart Cainite as Thot pointed out woven in to a normal sentence with emphasizing the Command<br /> And even the obvious &quot;Kneel before Zod!&quot; case the vampire in question can't be sure he did it because of common sense and survival intincts kicked in or because he was dominated to do it<br /> It is surpisingly subtile power and the best to pass notes to the player or pull him aside to discuss the scene (especially if you want the rest of the players remain unaware what really happened)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T11:26:13-08:00","id":1547492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay?p=1547487#post1547487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as Thot pointed out</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is a forum, shouldn't I at least be classified as an &quot;E-Thot&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T14:05:09-08:00","id":1547499,"title":"","content":"So, yes, sure there are nuances as there are different Dominate powers, I'm inquiring more how other ST prefer to handle it. I remember one discussion I had years ago with other Storytellers regarding the nature of powers like Dominate in games. A friend of mine used to argue that, in general, for most players, being dominated is sometimes worse than having a character destroyed by superior forces in combat and the like. To kind of &quot;take the Player's Character and make him do something&quot; seems to be considered by many players the worst thing, because it takes away their agency. That's basically the main reason why I ask how different STs prefer to handle it. I like the idea of giving cards/private messages to players, it's interesting to keep the mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T10:47:04-08:00","id":1547519,"title":"","content":"Subtle uses of dominate tend to go unnoticed, at least by the person being dominated.<br /> <br /> More obvious uses of dominate tend to shock the victim into asking, &quot;Why did I do that?&quot; afterwards, but sometimes the victim might rationalize their behavior. (e.g. &quot;I was too tired to resist.&quot; or &quot;He has such a magnetic personality I couldn't help but do as he asked.&quot; or &quot;You know, you had to be there, he was just so dominant.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Resisted attempts of dominate (the victim spends WP to resist) almost always results in the victim realizing some supernatural power is being used.<br /> <br /> Outside observers of the scene increasingly realize something is wrong if they are paying close attention, but may miss subtle uses of dominate. In much vampire media, when the vampire commands their victim, it is usually clear to the audience and other observers what is happening.<br /> <br /> = = = = =<br /> In terms of how I would run it as ST with its use against players, I use several ways.<br /> <br /> 1) If it is just a subtle use, I just have the NPC command or request the PC to do it and see if they do it anyway (many players are willing for their characters to accommodate reasonable requests). Only if they don't, do I say they are compelled but can spend WP to resist.<br /> <br /> 2) More outright uses of dominate against them, I go straight to the dominate rules. If the PC fails, I narrate what they do. They don't have much autonomy as they are under a kind of mesmeric spell so they can't do passive aggressive things and the like while being commanded. I do let players make OOC suggestions though about the scene if it improves the game.<br /> <br /> 3) I do have NPCs sometimes subsequently command the PC to forget what they just did (if they have Forgetful Mind) to again allow the player to resist. I want the player to know what happen. I have enough good, mature players now that generally they don't metagame these things. They enjoy the complications that occur. Keeping things above board and not confusing players gives more advantages than disadvantages in my experience, at least with my gaming groups.<br /> <br /> 4) I tend not to pass notes or take players aside anymore because the other players always suspect some form of mind control is going on. So I'm just open about it with the idea that we all want to create the best &quot;story&quot; together. If there is information I don't want other players to know, but one player needs to know, I do speak to them in private, but I try to limit such things.<br /> <br /> 5) In cases where a sire or other background elder has Conditioning, and could have implanted commands on the PC prior to the beginning of the chronicle, I work out the details in advance with the player. Typically I keep them limited to things like, &quot;If you are involved in a Masquerade breach or observe others doing so, when you have the first safe and secret opportunity when alone you will call this number and explain what has happened and forget that you did.&quot; It is not unusual for Ventrue and Tremere PCs to start a chronicle with something like this, but it is also not unusual for them to NOT have pre-planted commands. For other clans, it really depends on what kind of backstory and preludes the character has.<br /> <br /> 6) In some cases where I intend the NPC will command the PC to do something and then make them forget, I will ask the player if they want to know what they did, or if they just prefer not to know so there is some mystery. Or in more unusual cases, not give them that option at all to know what they did (although I do allow resisted dice rolls).<br /> <br /> In general, my principles are:<br /> 1) Make it known it is Dominate so they can spend WP if they so choose, and that they aren't confused by what is going on.<br /> 2) Quickly adjudicate the scene as players dislike not having agency so I want to get the scene quickly back to the point where they can act again.<br /> 3) Keep the player informed about what is going on, even if their PC is clueless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T21:23:32-08:00","id":1547535,"title":"","content":"While Dominate isn't my favorite Discipline, it can be used with great discretion in tandem with Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T22:04:38-08:00","id":1547538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay?p=1547519#post1547519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Subtle uses of dominate tend to go unnoticed, at least by the person being dominated.<br /> <br /> More obvious uses of dominate tend to shock the victim into asking, &quot;Why did I do that?&quot; afterwards, but sometimes the victim might rationalize their behavior. (e.g. &quot;I was too tired to resist.&quot; or &quot;He has such a magnetic personality I couldn't help but do as he asked.&quot; or &quot;You know, you had to be there, he was just so dominant.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Resisted attempts of dominate (the victim spends WP to resist) almost always results in the victim realizing some supernatural power is being used.<br /> <br /> Outside observers of the scene increasingly realize something is wrong if they are paying close attention, but may miss subtle uses of dominate. In much vampire media, when the vampire commands their victim, it is usually clear to the audience and other observers what is happening.<br /> <br /> = = = = =<br /> In terms of how I would run it as ST with its use against players, I use several ways.<br /> <br /> 1) If it is just a subtle use, I just have the NPC command or request the PC to do it and see if they do it anyway (many players are willing for their characters to accommodate reasonable requests). Only if they don't, do I say they are compelled but can spend WP to resist.<br /> <br /> 2) More outright uses of dominate against them, I go straight to the dominate rules. If the PC fails, I narrate what they do. They don't have much autonomy as they are under a kind of mesmeric spell so they can't do passive aggressive things and the like while being commanded. I do let players make OOC suggestions though about the scene if it improves the game.<br /> <br /> 3) I do have NPCs sometimes subsequently command the PC to forget what they just did (if they have Forgetful Mind) to again allow the player to resist. I want the player to know what happen. I have enough good, mature players now that generally they don't metagame these things. They enjoy the complications that occur. Keeping things above board and not confusing players gives more advantages than disadvantages in my experience, at least with my gaming groups.<br /> <br /> 4) I tend not to pass notes or take players aside anymore because the other players always suspect some form of mind control is going on. So I'm just open about it with the idea that we all want to create the best &quot;story&quot; together. If there is information I don't want other players to know, but one player needs to know, I do speak to them in private, but I try to limit such things.<br /> <br /> 5) In cases where a sire or other background elder has Conditioning, and could have implanted commands on the PC prior to the beginning of the chronicle, I work out the details in advance with the player. Typically I keep them limited to things like, &quot;If you are involved in a Masquerade breach or observe others doing so, when you have the first safe and secret opportunity when alone you will call this number and explain what has happened and forget that you did.&quot; It is not unusual for Ventrue and Tremere PCs to start a chronicle with something like this, but it is also not unusual for them to NOT have pre-planted commands. For other clans, it really depends on what kind of backstory and preludes the character has.<br /> <br /> 6) In some cases where I intend the NPC will command the PC to do something and then make them forget, I will ask the player if they want to know what they did, or if they just prefer not to know so there is some mystery. Or in more unusual cases, not give them that option at all to know what they did (although I do allow resisted dice rolls).<br /> <br /> In general, my principles are:<br /> 1) Make it known it is Dominate so they can spend WP if they so choose, and that they aren't confused by what is going on.<br /> 2) Quickly adjudicate the scene as players dislike not having agency so I want to get the scene quickly back to the point where they can act again.<br /> 3) Keep the player informed about what is going on, even if their PC is clueless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the ideas interesting. One thing is, if I'm not mistaken Dominate victims aren't allowd to spend WP to resist it anymore and there's a test to &quot;avoid eye contact&quot; (which I think it's fair, since that bs of wearing sunglasses in the 90's was a bit too ridiculous). Another point is that I often ask myself how much &quot;off game talk&quot; there should be in the game. In my early years as a ST I often used to make &quot;everything said after I start the game, besides tests results and things I state systematically as 'the Storyteller' is going to be considered 'in game', so mind your tongue and raise your hand if you want to talk 'off game'&quot; later, when I got older I got a little bit lazier and friendlier as a ST and I think sometimes the game suffers from it. So, to this day, I never know how much talk should be allowed during a game session. I fear off game knowledge affects the game way too much sometimes and it annoys me a lot. Sorry, I'm perhaps digressing a little. Thing is, sometimes I don't know if I should allow players to simply spend WP in order to resist Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T11:52:08-08:00","id":1547550,"title":"","content":"I am not up to all the V20 rules changes and TBH even 2e/Revised rules blend together in my mind, so I could be wrong on how WP can be used in terms of dominate. However, if you are worried that spending temporary WP is too powerful, then you could just require a reroll of the dice instead of an automatic resistance.<br /> <br /> I think spending temporary WP really depends on how much of a constrained resource it is. If the story chapters in the chronicle are short enough that temporary WP would never run out, then players aren't really making choices. If the chapters are long enough that it is possible for them to run out and not have it when it counts towards the end, then players will be more judicious when spending it.<br /> <br /> = = =<br /> My gaming groups are too undisciplined to not split between OOC and IC discussions. We just have too much fun making OOC comments. We just blend the two in back and forth. Usually it is easy to tell the difference, and when not, it is easy to clarify. My personal preference is to be focused on the game, but not everyone is the same and our goal is to have fun. There generally isn't any &quot;abuse&quot; of that because we're all honest and mature, and the rare times something happens that does cause me to raise an eyebrow, it's just better if I ignore it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T02:56:45-08:00","id":1547573,"title":"","content":"For my ST style I tend to tell the players <i>what their characters are feeling</i> and let them make the decisions from there, making willpower rolls/spending Willpower as appropriate. They are veteran players though, so are good at handling this sort of input.<br /> <br /> This is partially because I very much dislike the way that 'mind control' is handled in most film/tv as an unstoppable force. Handy for making the plot go the way you want it to as a writer, but kind of creepy for some of the audience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T11:44:56-08:00","id":1547715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay?p=1547573#post1547573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my ST style I tend to tell the players <i>what their characters are feeling</i> and let them make the decisions from there, making willpower rolls/spending Willpower as appropriate. They are veteran players though, so are good at handling this sort of input.<br /> <br /> This is partially because I very much dislike the way that 'mind control' is handled in most film/tv as an unstoppable force. Handy for making the plot go the way you want it to as a writer, but kind of creepy for some of the audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I use the same strategy, my games are usually &quot;psychologically heavy&quot; and my players are also veterans. Thing is, <i>Dominate</i> isn't much about your <i>feelings</i>, that's why I asked how other ST prefer to handle it. So it seems you like to tell your players <i>feel compeled</i> to act in a certain way? Do you always allow them to resist? If so, how? Spending WP or testing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T01:51:19-08:00","id":1547729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay?p=1547715#post1547715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I use the same strategy, my games are usually &quot;psychologically heavy&quot; and my players are also veterans. Thing is, <i>Dominate</i> isn't much about your <i>feelings</i>, that's why I asked how other ST prefer to handle it. So it seems you like to tell your players <i>feel compeled</i> to act in a certain way? Do you always allow them to resist? If so, how? Spending WP or testing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's usually down to the specifc circumstances so hard to give an example, especially as I tend not to put the protagonists in situations where they are dominated.<br /> <br /> That said I should expand on my earlier post. Where characters are being emotionally influenced, by Dementation for example, I tell them what they're feeling as above, and I usually try for a 'show not tell' approach describing the physical sensations of the emotional manipulation.<br /> <br /> Where characters are being mentally Dominated I would either tell them what they're thinking e.g. 'You have an overwhelming urge to get in the car', this tends to read like intrsuive thoughts though, or, I'll describe it with an emotional aspect e.g. 'Being in the car would make you feel much safer'.<br /> <br /> If they go against the thought/feeling I would allow it without a check but if the rules call for it make they pay a WP point<br /> <br /> If you want to posit a scenario then I can respond better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 01-14-2025, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T12:32:21-08:00","id":1547745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay?p=1547729#post1547729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's usually down to the specifc circumstances so hard to give an example, especially as I tend not to put the protagonists in situations where they are dominated.<br /> <br /> That said I should expand on my earlier post. Where characters are being emotionally influenced, by Dementation for example, I tell them what they're feeling as above, and I usually try for a 'show not tell' approach describing the physical sensations of the emotional manipulation.<br /> <br /> Where characters are being mentally Dominated I would either tell them what they're thinking e.g. 'You have an overwhelming urge to get in the car', this tends to read like intrsuive thoughts though, or, I'll describe it with an emotional aspect e.g. 'Being in the car would make you feel much safer'.<br /> <br /> If they go against the thought/feeling I would allow it without a check but if the rules call for it make they pay a WP point<br /> <br /> If you want to posit a scenario then I can respond better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, I tend to use a similar approach. Although reading &quot;...I tend not to put the protagonists in situations where they are dominated&quot; makes me wonder if you're that kind of ST who tend to avoid PCs destruction at all cost as well. I'm of the thinking that the PCs should be ready to deal with the consequences of their actions and I rarely ever give them &quot;plot armour&quot;, if the PCs end up being overwhelmed and/or destroyed they better learn the lesson not to deal with more than they can handle. Making the game seem like the PCs are always going to succeed no matter the odds tend to be much more damaging to the game than they losing a character or two (or three or twelve lol).<br /> <br /> Now regarding rules, Dominate tend to be much harsher than Presence when it comes to resisting it, in the early days there was this possibility of spending WP to resist, but it was 1 WP <b>per success</b> achieved by the cainite dominating them. In V20 they even eliminated this possibility and the character can only hope to avoid eye contact through a test.<br /> <br /> When it comes to examples of a scenario, I think a simple one that has probably happeneed in many many games around the world, say they are against a powerful kindred who dominate one of them to attack the others, how would you go about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T00:57:29-08:00","id":1547748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay?p=1547745#post1547745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how would you go about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't set up that situation in my story because it's divisive to the players and can only cause trouble. As I said before I find unbeatable mind control themes in stories to be cringeworthy at best and sickening at worst. It's the same reason why I despise rape elements in stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T07:04:17-08:00","id":1547754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay?p=1547748#post1547748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't set up that situation in my story because it's divisive to the players and can only cause trouble. As I said before I find unbeatable mind control themes in stories to be cringeworthy at best and sickening at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like an implementation problem of the mechanic rather than an issue with the mechanic itself.<br /> <br /> From your above comment, Dominate is only being used in very a direct, crude, and tactless manner. The mesmerize implanted command doesn't have any requirement for the command to be harmful, demeaning, or rapey. A good example comes from the books where a vampire left a command in random street vendors, cabbies, and other people out and about during the night to call a phone number of his if they see anything weird. As a result, the vampire had essentially an early warning system if a pack of sabbat or other supernaturals came into town, potentially even covering the daylights hours as well.<br /> <br /> Dominate is a tool, what you choose to do with that tool is a reflection of the wielder. A knife cuts, that's all. But a knife can fuel life by preparing food, it can save life by being a surgeons tool, it can protect life by helping you build a shelter, it can end life by being used as a weapon, or it can be used as a tool for compliance with the threat of its use.<br /> <br /> All the negativity around Dominate is in your head, and the psychological issues of losing control. If your players have that issue as well, then you haven't gained enough trust with them to return their characters largely unharmed if you use a Dominate NPC against them. Gaining this trust takes time and getting them comfortable with occasionally having the PCs controlled for a moment or perhaps a scene is something you work up to. But if they are so twitchy about control that they can't handle the iconic hypnotist gag of making the target cluck like a chicken without blowing a gasket, then they don't need a personal horror RPG, they need therapy.<br /> <br /> An Elder vampire could implant a command that activates a behavior which could save the target. A Tremere could implant a security phrase in the targets head that they will answer with when asked a specific question. This way the magical construct doesn't destroy the PCs if they visit the chantry, with the added benefit that the PCs have no way of giving the pass phrase to someone else since they technically don't know it.<br /> <br /> Don't like Magic &amp; Thaumaturgy, no problem. Consider if the command was used in relation to specific images, like the tv scene lock used in Johnny Pneumonic, the weird psychedelic patterns used in that Babylon 5 episode with the cyber assassin, or the visual activation technique or verbal deactivation code used on River in the Serenity movie.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if you want to go high humanity use, consider a &quot;therapist&quot; who only see's clients after dark, but has an amazing success rate with getting clients to alter their behaviors like to stop smoking, to stick with an exercise routine, etc. Anything that has a stimulus and reaction combination can be a potential story hook or behavior modification in the PCs. <br /> <br /> You are fighting an ideology around the idea of control, rather than dealing with how control itself is often an illusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T07:18:48-08:00","id":1547756,"title":"","content":"On a side note, Dominate isn't unbeatable. In fact, as you get closer to the modern age it gets weaker and weaker.<br /> <br /> It requires direct in person eye contact, a shared language, and the correct Generation level if applicable. Dominate doesn't work over telephones or video calls so telepresence business calls are going to be all the rage for vampires concerned with dominate issues. Likewise the use of cyberwarfare and drones short circuits a lot of classical vampire strategies as far as power.<br /> <br /> As for the language thing, to use a real world example a teacher used the word &quot;nigete&quot; in class. A few of the students thought the word sounded too close to a racial slur and got the teacher suspended. If a vampire used the first Dominate power a told you to &quot;nigete&quot; you wouldn't run away under compulsion, you would confused at best or getting ready for a brawl at worst, unless your spoke japanese of course.<br /> <br /> Dominate is an unbeatable threat if the only tactic the players consider using to trying to punch the enemy in the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T12:57:40-08:00","id":1547764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay?p=1547748#post1547748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't set up that situation in my story because it's divisive to the players and can only cause trouble. As I said before I find unbeatable mind control themes in stories to be cringeworthy at best and sickening at worst. It's the same reason why I despise rape elements in stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, after reading that I thought about answering, but then <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar727_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"727\" data-vbnamecard=\"727\">Thoth</a> summarized well a good part of what my response would be: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if they are so twitchy about control that they can't handle the iconic hypnotist gag of making the target cluck like a chicken without blowing a gasket, then they don't need a personal horror RPG, they need therapy. </div> </div> </div> Beyond that, I'm flabbergasted at best at your commentary, it's hard to express how I feel, I mean how can someone and a group limit themselves and their stories so much is beyond me. I mean, it's a <i>World of Darkness</i>, perhaps the group should consider playing something different because, well, I don't even know what to say anymore. Perhaps therapy is really the best way to go, because I simply can't get it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T16:35:41-08:00","id":1547767,"title":"","content":"So for me in shorter more blunt bursts no one cares.(Ignoring the obvious like such as crossing any lines.) If the antagonist is basically using dominate to get the mcguffin and make the party leave the building; then its just roll the save and the results will tell how much of a good idea that sounds like to the afflicted. <br /> <br /> For longer stuff when it was going to be a major factor in the game, I asked a bunch of questions to limit the odds that I crossed any lines and to make sure they knew what was expected in turn. Ie If a player is requesting their character's family not to be harmed, tormented, dominated, blood bound etc. I respect that so long as they don't start abusing that courtesy. This also allowed me to calibrate some other things like if in universe your character is secretly leaving info drops for an adversary do they want to know that's going on so they can get in on it, or is this a case of the reveal happening and suddenly they check their sent messages and there's a lot of responses they don't recall sending etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-16T01:12:29-08:00","id":1547774,"title":"","content":"I'm rather insulted by Thoth and Herr Meister so I'm going to drop this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-16T11:16:08-08:00","id":1547779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547463-how-do-you-see-dominated-characters-roleplay?p=1547774#post1547774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm rather insulted by Thoth and Herr Meister so I'm going to drop this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Objective facts &amp; basic intro to psychology which disproves your viewpoint = insult<br /> <br /> Might I suggest that being a politician, activist, or moderator could be promising career choices?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-16T19:51:12-08:00","id":1547794,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Please do not insult or attack other users and their preferences. Do not criticize another table's safety or calibration practices. Refrain from casting therapy in a negative light. Keep it civil, please. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-17T16:27:22-08:00","id":1547805,"title":"","content":"What if you could dominate a mortal, but, they gave you attitude? Or, you got one success or botched, so, what ever you command them to do, they do the opposite, so, you have to tell them the opposite of what you want them to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-17T17:14:59-08:00","id":1547808,"title":"","content":"It kinda goes against the point of botches if you can recover from a botch by just declaring the opposite of what you intended so the botch turns into a success.<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> That said, I really do think it's worth looking at VtR 2e's implementation of of Dominate as a way to balance player agency, mind control, pop culture vampire powers being in the game, and encouraging more creativity and subtlety in Dominate use.<br /> <br /> The main differences:<br /> <br /> 1) Dominate is a Clan &quot;signature&quot; Discipline, rather than being a common Discipline, this means it's much rarer in the general vampire population, and it's more predictable who has it. Given the in-universe requirements for learning Disciplines, and that Dominate works better on vampires that have had some of the user's blood, a lot of vampires aren't willing to take the risk.<br /> <br /> 2) There isn't the Generation disparity. While older vampires are more resistant broadly and will have an edge, since a neonate Ventrue has the chance of using Dominate on the Prince, vampires that toss Dominate around on their peers too often or too openly are rarely tolerated because it can escalate tensions so quickly.<br /> <br /> 3) VtR 2e's Dominate is a great example of how the Conditions/Beats system can really help things even if CofD 2e broadly doesn't keep that as tightly designed as it could have. The first power of its version of the Discipline inflicts the Mesmerized Condition, which is the basis of using the higher level powers on the target. This has two major impacts. First, there's XP for going a long with Dominate and resolving Mesmerized (or later Dominated) by doing the tasks demanded of your character, which helps blunt the lose of agency. Second, the Mesmerized Condition can be broken by taking damage or being ordered to perform an action that's a breaking point (so for PC vampires, that means going against their current Humanity rating). So Dominating your enemies makes them stronger, and if you don't study them carefully, you might not even get your commands followed because you ask things that ruin the Mesmerized chain.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure this is good enough for people that have a strong aversion of full mind-control on PCs, but it can certainly help for groups with a weak aversion to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}